From 448731f02b0fc569a819eba74457667d1ee52ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Romanov <romanovda@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:25:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ZDC try X7: photon-core split of the ZDC imaging clusters,
 cluster floor 20 MeV, refit

Phase 4 (the Lambda bar fight), experiment X7_core_split, build label X7, on X5 (baked, 57b698c4).
ImagingTopoCluster gets a photon-core split (coreSplitSeedEdep, default off; other detectors unchanged):
a saved group is split between its shallow energy cores - local maxima of at least the seed energy in
the first coreSplitMaxLayer layers, the more energetic of two cores closer than coreSplitMinDistXY kept -
and one shared region seeded by every deeper maximum; hits join the region of their most energetic
neighbour in decreasing energy. The ZDC uses seeds of 5 MeV in the first 4 layers, 50 mm apart, and a
cluster floor of 20 MeV (was 50). Calibration refit on D2/D3 for this clustering (scripts/420,
space/perf/calib-SCAN_X7cal.json): photon 4.496*E^0.848, neutron 6.214*E^0.740.
Scans (two D4 files, X5's calibration): split + floor 20 MeV gives 712 / 716 truth-matched Lambda at
150 / 275 GeV against X5's 480 / 492; clean three-cluster events 0.50 vs 0.28.
Prediction: S4a_tm per thrown Lambda -> n pi0 = 6.4 % mean over 100-275 GeV and 11.8 % at 275 GeV
(X5: 4.373 % / 8.030 %). Judged against X5_photon_depth_face.
Verdict: pending (recorded in the next commit on this branch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
